  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-04-20T15:35:51.007Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "You reach Trusted! Yay!! ... Now what? It's a nice title, pretty color for your profile, but that's about it. With the trust ranks, nothing is pulling someone in, saying \"hey, you wanna reach this rank.\" What if we could change that? Instances could be set to between this-rank and that-rank can join, or only this rank can join the instance (public, friends, or invite). Perhaps you could unlock features with higher trust ranks. One example could be that Trusted users could have the ability to change their profile picture, but only so many times within a time period (such as once every month). I'd be curious to what other people could add-on or elaborate with this topic.",
